112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 91 0 R
/T (Participants will be provided with a predefined component list, PCB design constraints, and a reference image with exact dimensions of the Line Follower chassis. The objective is to create a compact, optimized PCB that fits within the specified mechanical boundaries while ensuring reliable performance and clean signal routing. The PCB must be designed to accurately interface all provided components, ensuring proper power distribution, signal integrity, and efficient routing under given constraints. Special attention must be given to maintaining dimensional accuracy so that the PCB aligns closely with the provided chassis reference \(either identical or functionally equivalent in size and mounting compatibility\). )
/E (Participants will be provided with a predefined component list, PCB design constraints, and a reference image with exact dimensions of the Line Follower chassis. The objective is to create a compact, optimized PCB that fits within the specified mechanical boundaries while ensuring reliable performance and clean signal routing. The PCB must be designed to accurately interface all provided components, ensuring proper power distribution, signal integrity, and efficient routing under given constraints. Special attention must be given to maintaining dimensional accuracy so that the PCB aligns closely with the provided chassis reference \(either identical or functionally equivalent in size and mounting compatibility\). )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
